{{Quote|You are a fool. There's nothing magic about the mines of Mandalore. They supplied beskar ore to our ancestors and the rest is superstition.|Bo-Katan Kryze to Din Djarin|<ref name="Chapter 17" />}}
The '''Mines of Mandalore'''<ref name="Chapter 18">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 18: The Mines of Mandalore}}</ref> were located under the [[Civic Center]] in the [[city]] of [[Sundari]] on [[Mandalore]]. They supplied [[beskar]] [[ore]] to [[Mandalorian]]s, and were the site of the [[Living Waters]].<ref name="Chapter 17" /> According to the [[Mandalorian Creed]] of the [[Children of the Watch]], a Mandalorian [[Apostate (religion)|apostate]] could only be redeemed for removing their [[helmet]] by visiting the Living Waters.<ref name="Return of the Mandalorian" />

The mines existed thousands of years before the time of the [[New Republic]] and also during the time of the first Mandalore. According to ancient folklore, the mines were once a [[mythosaur]] lair, and [[Mandalore the Great]] tamed the mythical beast.<ref name="Chapter 18" /> By the [[time]] of the [[New Republic Era]], when Din Djarin revealed to [[the Armorer]] that he had taken off his helmet, she stated the only way for him to atone was to travel to the Mines of Mandalore and redeem himself in the Living Waters, although they were thought to be destroyed in the [[Great Purge of Mandalore]].<ref name="Return of the Mandalorian" /> [[Din Djarin]] believed the mines survived after he found a crystal from the surface of the planet that [[Jawa]]s traded with a traveler. According to [[Bo-Katan Kryze]], there was nothing magic about the mines except for supplying beskar ore to Mandalorians.<ref name="Chapter 17" />

Djarin went on a [[mission to the Living Waters]] to redeem himself and remove his [[decree of exile]].<ref name="Chapter 17" /> Eventually he was able to bathe in the Waters. However, he lost his consciousness and was rescued by Kryze, who witnessed a living mythosaur in the Waters,<ref name="Chapter 18" /> unbeknownst to Djarin. They later returned to the [[Mandalorian secret covert|covert]] to prove that Djarin was redeemed. [[Paz Vizsla]] doubted their claims, saying the mines were collapsed in the Purge. However, Djarin brought a proof from the Living Waters, and the Armorer confirmed its authenticity.<ref name="Chapter 19">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 19: The Convert}}</ref>

